# Project Context Rule

## Purpose
Keep all coding-agent work aligned with approved project artifacts and workflow intent.

## Source of Truth
- `project-spec/00-brief.md`
- `project-spec/02-prd.md`
- `project-spec/03-scope.md`
- `project-spec/04-user-stories.md`
- `project-spec/05-acceptance-criteria.md`
- `project-spec/09-done-definition.md`

## Core Workflow
Always align decisions to:
`Intake -> Clarify -> PRD -> Tasks -> Design Sync -> Handoff`

## Mandatory Behavior
- Do not implement features outside approved MVP scope.
- Treat unresolved clarifications as risk, not hidden assumptions.
- If requirements conflict, prefer approved PRD and acceptance criteria.
- Keep outputs deterministic and schema-friendly.

## Delivery Orientation
- Prioritize artifact quality over prompt creativity.
- Preserve versionability of generated documents and task updates.
- Keep human review as a hard gate before export.

## Optional: Superpowers (Cursor plugin)
- When the Superpowers plugin is enabled in Cursor, prefer its skills for multi-step work (e.g. planning before large changes, systematic debugging, verification before claiming done).
- Rules in this repo and paths under `project-spec/` remain authoritative; Superpowers reinforces discipline, it does not replace approved specs.
- If Superpowers is not installed, follow the same discipline using these rules and artifacts alone.
